     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Each 3,000 mg dose is also about three times the usual single dose of 500\u20131,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of acute liver injury, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual ceiling)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nSome clinicians cap the daily total at 3,000 mg for prolonged use. Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still recommend pharmacy review first."
      }
     ],
